      "originalRationaleParagraphs": [
        "Mandatory aspect-1 and aspect-2 plus fresh independent transfer/variation rules remain. New aspect-2 and source-required-assay/evidence-not-run-quota axes consistently distinguish assay-method route from ketose-extension scope. A Benedict choice alone is no longer treated as proof that fructose tautomerism is required.",
        "The retained fructose/enediol-to-aldose teaching model is an explicit appropriate-route extension. It is not certified as an exhaustive elementary mechanism, made universal to every basic route, or used to infer all other jurisdictions were reviewed. The original HE basic/elevated distinction remains the source boundary.",
        "The corrected cases and raw-profile axes explicitly permit rich coherent independently performed work with genuine distinct transfer to cover several requirements. They forbid an additional run solely to meet a fixed quota after adequate evidence. The unchanged aspect-1 historical Doppellauf/two-run wording is an available workflow reference; the explicit current whole-case and axis rules prevent it being used as a compulsory extra-run quota."
      ],
